\section{The distributional parameters}{

\code{mu} is \code{gamma_0} and every other coefficient is \code{gamma1}, \code{gamma2},
and so on, all with identity links. There are \code{df + 1} of them.

A formula on \code{mu} is the proportional-hazards (or -odds, or -probit)
model, because \code{gamma_0} shifts the whole curve. A formula on any
other coefficient is a TIME-VARYING effect, since that coefficient
multiplies a function of log time; this is what \code{flexsurv} spells
\verb{anc =}.

